        "content": "# Sinch Agent Tools Overview\n\n**Launch Date:** August 4, 2026\n\n**What It Does:**\nAgent Tools is a suite of integrations designed to help developers build, test, and deploy applications powered by Sinch's communication infrastructure platform directly within their preferred development environments and AI-assisted coding tools.\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n- **IDE Extensions**: Includes tools for Visual Studio Code, JetBrains-based environments, and Open VSX-compatible editors\n\n- **Simulator Mode**: Enables developers to test integrations from within their development environment before creating a Sinch account or making live API calls\n\n- **AI Assistant Support**: Compatible with Claude Code, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, and ChatGPT Desktop through an MCP server\n\n- **Structured Information Access**: Provides accurate API definitions and product knowledge across multiple Sinch services including:\n  - Conversation API\n  - Authentication\n  - Voice\n  - Verification\n  - Numbers\n  - Elastic SIP Trunking\n  - Fax\n  - Mailgun\n\n**How It Helps Developers:**\nThe platform reduces the need to switch between coding tools, documentation, and web portals. Developers can work within their existing workflows to explore and evaluate Sinch services without account setup, then implement and test integrations without leaving their preferred development environment.\n\nAgent Tools is available globally as part of Sinch's broader developer offering."
